* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Digital Dice — component and pin reference
* Transcribed from: hardware/schematic/digital-dice-schematic.pdf
* Source export   : "Digital Dice Fix", 20/12/2024, OhmFusion, Group 6
*
* This is a human-readable reference, not a machine netlist. It lists every
* component reference designator, its pin numbering, and the intended net for
* each pin. Use it alongside docs/ASSEMBLY.md when wiring the board.
*
* The two channels are electrically identical. Channel 1 drives the left
* display, channel 2 the right. Only the timing capacitor differs.
* -------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SUBCKT CHANNEL_1

* --- clock source ---------------------------------------------------------
U3    NE555      timing oscillator, astable
      pin 1  GND        ground
      pin 2  TR         tied to pin 6 (standard astable)
      pin 3  OUT        -> U2 pin 14 (CD4017 CLK)
      pin 4  R          tied to VCC (reset inactive)
      pin 5  CV         100 nF decoupling to GND (recommended, see ASSEMBLY)
      pin 6  TH         tied to pin 2
      pin 7  DC         junction of R1 and R2
      pin 8  VCC        +5 V

R1    5.1k       VCC to pin 7          charge path
R2    5.1k       pin 7 to pin 6/2      charge and discharge path
C2    10u        pin 6/2 to GND        timing capacitor — FAST channel

* --- sequencer ------------------------------------------------------------
U2    CD4017     decade counter, mod-6 by feedback
      pin 14 CLK        <- U3 pin 3
      pin 13 CE         GND (clock enable, active LOW)
      pin 15 MR         <- pin 5 (Q6) via R_RESET, pulled down by R2_PD
      pin 16 VDD        +5 V
      pin  8 VSS        GND
      pin  3 Q0         -> U5 in1                (digit 1)
      pin  2 Q1         -> U6 in1                (digit 2)
      pin  4 Q2         -> U5 in2, U6 in2        (digit 3)
      pin  7 Q3         -> U9 in1                (digit 4)
      pin 10 Q4         -> U5 in3, U9 in2        (digit 5)
      pin  1 Q5         -> U6 in3, U9 in3        (digit 6)
      pin  5 Q6         -> pin 15 (MR)  <-- this is what makes it mod-6
      pin  6 Q7         no connect
      pin  9 Q8         no connect
      pin 11 Q9         no connect
      pin 12 CO         no connect

R2_PD 1k         pin 15 to GND         MR pull-down, prevents floating reset

* --- combinational mapping ------------------------------------------------
* One CD4075 package contains all three gates below.
U5    OR_3       Q0 + Q2 + Q4  -> U1 pin 7  (BCD A, weight 1)
U6    OR_3       Q1 + Q2 + Q5  -> U1 pin 1  (BCD B, weight 2)
U9    OR_3       Q3 + Q4 + Q5  -> U1 pin 2  (BCD C, weight 4)
*                                  U1 pin 6  (BCD D, weight 8) -> GND

* --- display driver -------------------------------------------------------
U1    74LS47     BCD to seven-segment decoder, outputs ACTIVE LOW
      pin  7 A          <- U5 out
      pin  1 B          <- U6 out
      pin  2 C          <- U9 out
      pin  6 D          GND
      pin  3 LT         VCC   (lamp test inactive)
      pin  4 BI/RBO     VCC   (blanking inactive)
      pin  5 RBI        VCC   (ripple blanking inactive)
      pin 16 VCC        +5 V
      pin  8 GND        ground
      pin 13 Qa         -> display segment a, via 220R
      pin 12 Qb         -> display segment b, via 220R
      pin 11 Qc         -> display segment c, via 220R
      pin 10 Qd         -> display segment d, via 220R
      pin  9 Qe         -> display segment e, via 220R
      pin 15 Qf         -> display segment f, via 220R
      pin 14 Qg         -> display segment g, via 220R

* --- display --------------------------------------------------------------
DS1   7SEG-CA    common ANODE, one digit
      COM               +5 V
      a..g              <- U1 via series resistors

.ENDS CHANNEL_1

* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
.SUBCKT CHANNEL_2
* Identical to CHANNEL_1 with these substitutions:
*
*   U3  -> (second NE555)      U2 -> U4  (CD4017)
*   U1  -> U7  (74LS47)        U5 -> U8, U6 -> U11, U9 -> U12  (CD4075)
*   R2_PD -> R3  1k            C2 -> C1  100u   timing capacitor — SLOW channel
*
* The 10x difference between C1 and C2 is intentional: it is what gives the
* two displays "waktu spin berbeda" (different spin times) and stops the pair
* from behaving as a single die shown twice.
.ENDS CHANNEL_2

* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
* NOTES AND OPEN ITEMS
*
* 1. The schematic export lists R1 = 5.1k and a single 1k per channel. The
*    second 555 timing resistor is not separately annotated in the export.
*    The values above assume R1 = R2 = 5.1k, which yields 9.4 Hz on the fast
*    channel. Measure your own board before quoting figures.
*
* 2. At 9.4 Hz the fast channel reads as a flicker rather than a true blur.
*    See docs/THEORY.md, "Choosing the spin rate", for the recommended change
*    to 1-2.2 uF if you want the display to be genuinely unreadable mid-spin.
*
* 3. The original proposal (docs/Proposal-Awal-OhmFusion.pdf) specified
*    CD4026B, which integrates counter and segment driver. The final build
*    replaced it with CD4017 + CD4075 + 74LS47 to make the 1..6 restriction
*    explicit in discrete logic. See docs/THEORY.md, "Why not the CD4026".
*
* 4. Series resistors on the segment lines are REQUIRED. See ASSEMBLY.md.
* -------------------------------------------------------------------------
